Define a strategy shape and a registry:<br/><pre>type PricingStrategy = (base: number) => number;
const pricing: Record&lt;string, PricingStrategy&gt; = {
  free:       () =&gt; 0,
  basic:      (b) =&gt; b,
  pro:        (b) =&gt; b * 0.9,
  enterprise: (b) =&gt; b * 0.75,
};
function price(plan: string, base: number): number {
  const rule = pricing[plan];
  if (!rule) throw new Error(`unknown plan: ${plan}`);
  return rule(base);
}</pre>Prices are unchanged. A new plan is a single entry in <code>pricing</code> — no branch added to a growing function, and the existing four plans share no code path with it, so they don't need re-testing. Strategy is justified because the conditional already grew to four branches along the same 'plan' axis: the smell earned the pattern.

